<!--
    kuna `option iteregion` value `auto` (the default), P8 goto-quality: in a
    function the per-function detector (p3_dataflow/kuna_unoptimized.rs) calls
    unoptimized, how the raw block graph joins a conditional value
    (p8_structure/kuna_o0select.rs) decides whether it prints as `?:`.

    gcc 11 -O0 (-fno-pic -fno-stack-protector -fcf-protection=none) of
        extern void use(int);
        int pick(int c, int a, int b) { int x = c ? a : b; return x + 1; }
        int flag(int a, int b) { int x; if (a > b) x = 1; else x = 0; return x + 2; }
        void arg(int c, int a) { use(c ? a + 1 : 7); }
    pick's and arg's arms each load a register that is stored or passed once
    after the join; flag's arms each store to x.

    Pass 1 (default auto): pick prints its conditional value (#1), flag keeps
    its if/else (#2, #3) and arg's computed arm folds (#4). Pass 2 (option
    iteregion on, the old default): pick prints an if without an else (#5),
    flag's two constant stores fold into a conditional (#6) and arg keeps its
    if/else (#7).
-->
